      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T00:55:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We can go back to previous version of this CL (which was checking if only timer interrupt is pending)\n\nI think this one sounds like a good choice for now, so that we can deploy this fix and see if it fixes the bug. In parallel we should:\n\n* File a bug and assign to FPC to see what calculation they are doing triggers an exception.\n* Create a separate CL that adds a handler for FPU events. This could be useful for debugging. Maybe we have other floating point code in EC that silently triggers exceptions? What happens if you intentionally do a divide by zero (with floating point) with the current code?",
      "parentUuid": "e071f14a_86cbde60",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 506,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 507,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "4e8ccc5a890284e550d070914db9a28776162346",
