      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T13:42:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What happens if you intentionally do a divide by zero (with floating point) with the current code?\n\nI used the following code\n```\nstatic int command_test(int argc, char **argv)\n{\n        float zero \u003d 0.0f;\n        float one \u003d 1.0f;\n        float div;\n        asm volatile(\n                \"fdivs %0, %1, %2\"\n                : \"\u003dw\"(div)\n                : \"w\"(one),  \"w\"(zero)\n        );\n\n        return EC_SUCCESS;\n}\nDECLARE_CONSOLE_COMMAND(test, command_test, \"\", \"\");\n```\n\nAfter calling this, FPU interrupt become pending but EC is still running",
      "parentUuid": "211daa29_4fb33940",
      "range": {
